WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.252
Hi, I'm Birch!

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:06.100
Beacon records what your coding agents do, then asks a decision model

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.703
which runs to learn from.

00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:13.591
Most setups put a decision model inside the loop.

00:00:13.591 --> 00:00:17.705
Beacon grades finished runs offline, and turns promising ones into skills.

00:00:19.508 --> 00:00:24.413
Beacon captures sessions from twenty-nine harnesses, through hooks, pollers and a browser

00:00:24.413 --> 00:00:26.865
extension, into one typed event stream.

00:00:27.285 --> 00:00:31.043
A finished trace, cut to six fields per event, goes to a

00:00:31.043 --> 00:00:32.921
decision model with three yes-or-no questions.

00:00:33.341 --> 00:00:35.061
The three probabilities are averaged.

00:00:35.061 --> 00:00:38.845
At zero point six or above, it becomes a review candidate.

00:00:39.265 --> 00:00:41.397
A person approves or rejects each candidate.

00:00:41.397 --> 00:00:43.834
Nothing in the loop approves on its own.

00:00:44.254 --> 00:00:48.414
Approved runs become skill files future agents load, and those sessions are

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:49.800
captured and scored again.

00:00:51.192 --> 00:00:52.565
The whole gate is one line.

00:00:53.192 --> 00:00:55.261
Success: did the run complete its task?

00:00:56.238 --> 00:00:58.549
Reuse: is there a correction worth passing on?

00:00:59.285 --> 00:01:01.505
Evidence: do the trace's events back it up?

00:01:02.915 --> 00:01:07.330
A plain average against a fixed constant: no single answer can veto a run.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:12.093
The model is asked whether the task succeeded, and whether the

00:01:12.093 --> 00:01:13.254
run holds a correction.

00:01:13.674 --> 00:01:17.726
But every event records exit codes, actors and approvals exactly, and

00:01:17.726 --> 00:01:19.200
the projection drops them.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.779
Only the reuse question needs a model.

00:01:23.592 --> 00:01:27.977
The project's own dashboard: a thousand and twenty-five events, a thousand and

00:01:27.977 --> 00:01:29.439
fifteen from one harness.

00:01:29.859 --> 00:01:33.855
Here, a hundred and sixty-seven approvals, each counted as a typed field.

00:01:35.225 --> 00:01:38.892
Let the record answer what it knows exactly; spend the model only

00:01:38.892 --> 00:01:41.642
on what a regex can't: is this lesson reusable?

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:47.820
Capture everything, grade finished runs after the loop, and let a person

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.454
decide what becomes a skill.

00:01:49.874 --> 00:01:51.880
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:52.453
I'm Birch.

00:01:52.453 --> 00:01:52.739
Bye!
